<title>ITALY: Brazil Bombril to take over Cirio.</title>
<headline>Brazil Bombril to take over Cirio.</headline>
<dateline>ROME 1997-04-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Brazilian company Bombril SA will take a controlling stake in Italian food processing firm Cirio Finanziaria Spa by the end of April, the Cragnotti group which owns both companies said on Monday.</p>
<p>Group chairman Sergio Cragnotti said he would meet the board of Bombril in Brazil on Tuesday to discuss the transaction.</p>
<p>&quot;Tomorrow the board of Bombril should approve a $300 million capital input for the acquisition of Cirio,&quot; Cragnotti told a news conference.</p>
<p>Cirio, Italy's largest food processing firm, was bought by Cragnotti &amp; Partners in 1994.</p>
<p>-- Rome Newsroom +39 6 678 2505</p>
</text>
